ac{3}{4}\\cdot 1=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\n- Finally, after a vertical shift of $2$ units up, we get a point with the $y$-coordinate\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3}{4}+2=\\frac{11}{4}.\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo find the $y$-intercept, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{3}{4}{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{0}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 1+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\frac{3}{4}{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x}+2$ intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,\\frac{11}{4}).$" 13194139533645 true] [17592186243819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243820 13194139533645 true] [17592186243819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243821 13194139533645 true] [17592186243819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243822 13194139533645 true] [17592186243819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243823 13194139533645 true] [17592186243819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243824 13194139533645 true] [17592186243819 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533645 true] [17592186243819 1041 "selection" 13194139533645 true] [17592186243819 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243821 13194139533645 true] [17592186243819 1110 #uuid "afa7549d-2c8a-5773-9b7c-8c6510e8f8ad" 13194139533645 true] [17592186243820 1034 "(0,\\frac{3}{4})" 13194139533645 true] [17592186243820 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533645 true] [17592186243820 1111 #uuid "8fe37f75-e5f0-5c88-b657-109020923936" 13194139533645 true] [17592186243821 1034 "(0,\\frac{11}{4})" 13194139533645 true] [17592186243821 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533645 true] [17592186243821 1111 #uuid "6ebb5fe3-ab18-57e7-8377-1e1057378c4c" 13194139533645 true] [17592186243822 1034 "(0,-\\frac{5}{4})" 13194139533645 true] [17592186243822 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533645 true] [17592186243822 1111 #uuid "cb552c2d-234b-5035-9ee4-d877ce5d5285" 13194139533645 true] [17592186243823 1034 "(-\\frac{5}{4},0)" 13194139533645 true] [17592186243823 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533645 true] [17592186243823 1111 #uuid "f55909bb-907b-515c-a42a-3b017c53704e" 1319413